First, let us run the command ls to see what files are there. We see flag.txt, meaning the flag is probably in there. When we run cat flag.txt, it says permission denied, due to our user not having access to the file. Let us now take a look at what files we have access to. This can be done by using the command sudo, which allows us to execute actions on other accounts’ privileges, most often the root’s.

